{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgbp4cpKBzy78wEJqTBuz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KCB2PUfdfbKTVKErnJfiVP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work && ./board show | tail -8 && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\n \"candidate\": \"Si\",\n \"family\": \"eval_general\",\n \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n \"value\": 5.467,\n \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"uncertainty\": 0.001,\n \"method\": {\n  \"engine\": \"ALCHEMI (nvalchemi-toolkit 0.2.0 MACEWrapper, batched GPU); cross-check with mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator\",\n  \"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 (medium), float64\",\n  \"protocol\": \"static 0 K E(V) scan of the diamond-cubic cell (17 points, isotropic strain +/-2/4/6% around a=5.43 A) + 3rd-order Birch-Murnaghan EOS fit; Vinet/Murnaghan fits and ASE BFGS+FrechetCellFilter cell relaxation (fmax 1e-5) as checks\",\n  \"ensemble\": \"static lattice (0 K, no zero-point or thermal vibrations)\",\n  \"timestep_fs\": null,\n  \"n_atoms\": 8,\n  \"sim_length_ps\": null,\n  \"seeds\": 1,\n  \"eos_form\": \"birchmurnaghan\",\n  \"bulk_modulus_GPa\": 87.4,\n  \"supercell_check_n_atoms\": 64\n },\n \"flags\": [],\n \"note\": \"Best estimate a0 = 5.467 A (BM3, +/-4% window: 5.4666 A; +/-2% window: 5.4673 A; ASE cell relaxation: 5.4674 A; 64-atom supercell: identical to 8-atom; residual pressure at 5.4666 A = 0.04 GPa, i.e. ~0.001 A). The uncertainty (0.001 A) covers only the numerical part: EOS form (BM3/Vinet/Murnaghan), fit window (2-6%), cell size, and code path (spread 5.4654-5.4674 A). It does NOT cover model error. The model is trained on PBE data and gives the PBE-level answer, not the experimental one: it is +0.036 A (+0.66%) above the CODATA 2018 Si lattice parameter 5.431020511(89) A (22.5 C, vacuum; NIST CODATA X-ray values), consistent with PBE's known ~0.6% overestimate for Si. Validation with the same setup recovers known PBE-type trends: Ge 5.720 A vs experimental 5.6574 A (+1.1%; PBE is reported to overestimate Ge by >1%); Cu 3.639 A (published PBE ~3.63 A, from a secondary source); Al 4.038 A; diamond C 3.578 A. Zero-point and thermal expansion to 295 K were not computed; they would shift the value slightly upward, by a few mA, so the PBE bias dominates the gap to experiment. For a property compared to experiment, use about +/-0.04 A as the realistic total uncertainty. Scripts: /work/scripts/eos.py, /work/scripts/ase_check.py; raw fits: /work/run/eos_results.json.\"\n}\nEOF\npython -I -c \"import json;json.load(open('/work/run/result.json'));print('json ok')\"","description":"Recheck board and prepare result payload"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2835,"cache_read_input_tokens":39999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2835,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82463fa6-9dd8-4dde-b06a-fb4d94bf525a","uuid":"ea7a14ec-ff38-4913-ad6b-c23c9e513a78","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:27:35.000Z","request_id":"req_011Cgbp4c5AWdjEQFytiPh2a","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KCB2PUfdfbKTVKErnJfiVP":{"command":"cd /work && ./board show | tail -8 && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\n \"candidate\": \"Si\",\n \"family\": \"eval_general\",\n \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n \"value\": 5.467,\n \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n \"uncertainty\": 0.001,\n \"method\": {\n  \"engine\": \"ALCHEMI (nvalchemi-toolkit 0.2.0 MACEWrapper, batched GPU); cross-check with mace-torch 0.3.15 ASE calculator\",\n  \"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 (medium), float64\",\n  \"protocol\": \"static 0 K E(V) scan of the diamond-cubic cell (17 points, isotropic strain +/-2/4/6% around a=5.43 A) + 3rd-order 